e institution and  about today's event so thank you very  much  [Applause]  thanks Brian and before we connect to  Jessica I just want to join Brian in  welcoming all of you from Fulton and  from Memorial preparatory we are really  pleased to share this day with you I  hope you're as excited as I am and all  of us at Scripps art science can really  take you to some amazing places and in  the little film we saw of Jessica under  the ice and Antarctica and slithering  through narrow places into caves those  are great examples but look where she is  now she's going to be speaking to us  from space and we hope that that you're  as excited about science being able to  take you these kinds of places as we are  so Jessica welcome back to Scripps  Margaret line in here as well as a  hundred and fifty middle school students  from Fulton k-8 and Memorial preparatory  and of course a lot of your friends and  supporters from here at Scripps and the  UC San Diego community and as director I  want to make sure you know how proud we  are of everything that you've done with  this extraordinary background in  oceanography and being able to realize  this dream of yours to go to space and  we know that you're doing a lot of  science up there and thank you so much  for taking time out of busy schedule to  talk with us back here in San Diego  thank you so much Brian and Margaret it  and hello to all of the Fulton and  memorial students and all of my  colleagues and friends back at Scripps  it really means so much for me to be  able to share my life up here with all  of you it really is one of the big  objectives of my mission is to share  this experience with as many people as I  can because I am so incredibly fortunate  to be up here I don't want to take any  time away from the great students of the  questions have to ask so I think we  should just get right into those great  to Jessica and Brian is going to lead us  in taking care of the questions Brian  Thank You Margot thank you so 